Aerie-Purpose: Let a folder, or Settings, open a link that the page asked to open in a new tab in the page's own tab instead, and put a new tab next to its opener inside a folder that says so.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/navigator (browser_navigator.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #141. chrome::Navigate calls aerie_tab_model::HandleLinkOpen (overlay,
chrome/browser/aerie_tab_model/links_open_hook.h) after its shutdown checks and before it does anything
else. The call changes something only for one case: Chromium has already made the contents of a page-requested
new tab (a link with target=_blank, or window.open without window features), the disposition is
NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB, the contents has no opener, a user gesture started it, and "Links open" for the source tab
is "in place" (the nearest folder that sets it, else aerie.tabs.links_open). Then it navigates the source tab to
the address with a second chrome::Navigate (CURRENT_TAB), drops the new contents, and returns true, and this
call returns nullptr. Ctrl+click, Shift+click, middle-click, "Open link in new tab", popups and window.open with
features have other dispositions or no contents, and a window.open call that keeps window.opener has an opener:
none of these is touched. When the value is "in a new tab" and a folder sets it, the call only tells the tab
strip adapter to file the next new tab inside that folder, next to the source tab, and returns false. The header
has no dependencies, so the new dep of :impl cannot make a cycle; the definition is in links_open_hook.cc.

